  "notes": [
    "The anchor and the other migrations were sent by Four.meme's migration keeper 0x74d86638, but each ran the defect on a pool attacker EOAs 0x010fc97c/0x907004b6 had pre-initialized, and the BNB went to unaffiliated drainers, so they are exploit transactions, not affiliated rescues (rule 5).",
    "Campaign: every keeper migration that deposited 1 wei of token into a pre-initialized pool (74 in total, none before the anchor or after block 46557131) and, per pool, the first swap taking at least half its WBNB; earlier attacker pool setups never migrated.",
    "Loss is what those first drains took from the 68 drained pools (loss.mjs, pools as victims). Six pools drained later (about 7 BNB) and the locker's 0.4% fee are left out; measured at the launchpad instead, the deposits into the 74 pools total 376.06 BNB."
  ],
